import { BytesInspectionCopy } from "../model"

pub fn copy -> BytesInspectionCopy = BytesInspectionCopy {
  summary: "empty creates Bytes containing no bytes. Call it as bytes.empty (), where () is the value of the Unit type.",
  taskTitle: "Create an empty byte sequence and compare it with one byte",
  purpose: "Keep using Bytes even when there is no content. The same function displays Empty for an empty sequence and Bytes: [65] for a sequence containing the single byte 65.",
  typescriptBefore: "In TypeScript, new Uint8Array() creates an empty byte sequence, and length === 0 detects it. The one-byte case validates 65 before passing it to Uint8Array.of(value). Constructing a typed array is not itself a check that rejects out-of-range numbers.",
  benefit: "The empty and nonempty cases use the same Bytes type. Check for emptiness with isEmpty. empty creates an ordinary Bytes value with zero elements, rather than a failure or a missing value.",
  setup: "import * as bytes makes std/bytes available through the alias bytes. fn describe content: bytes.Bytes -> String accepts Bytes named content and returns a string. Calls pass arguments after spaces, as in describe content.",
  after: [
    "bytes.empty () passes the Unit value () to empty and creates empty Bytes. In describe (bytes.empty ()), the parentheses obtain that Bytes value first and then pass it to describe.",
    "The if bytes.isEmpty content then ... else ... in describe returns the first string for empty content and the second otherwise. isEmpty returns Bool. Here, the empty sequence produces Empty.",
    "The do { ... } in main runs its steps from top to bottom. After displaying the empty sequence, it validates bytes.byte 65. That returns Either<ByteError, Byte>, with Left for failure and Right for success.",
    "The match branch Left error gives the failure the name error and turns it into a string with show. Right checked names the successful Byte checked, then bytes.singleton checked makes one-byte Bytes. It does not pass the Int literal 65 straight to singleton.",
    "In the nonempty branch, bytes.toInts content returns an array of integers and show makes a display String. The ${...} in the backtick string inserts that result, so the second line is Bytes: [65].",
  ],
  details: [
    "empty takes Unit and returns Bytes. Just pass (); no source array or validation result is needed. There is no Either or Maybe to unpack to obtain the empty result.",
    "Empty Bytes is different from Bytes containing a single byte whose value is 0. isEmpty returns True for the former and False for the latter. It checks whether there are zero elements, rather than checking their values.",
    "You can also use the result of empty as an empty sequence in append or concat. Joining an empty sequence contributes no new elements.",
  ],
}
